  "citation": "Barad, M.L. (1958). Project Prairie Grass, A Field Program in Diffusion. AFCRL-TR-58-235. Run 29: stability D-E, arc-maximum SO2 concentrations at 50-800 m.",
  "dataConfidence": "High",
  "description": "Prairie Grass Run 29. Slightly stable (E) conditions: Q=41.5 g/s SO2 at 0.46 m height, U(2m)=3.94 m/s, dT=-0.78 C. Flat short-grass prairie, z0=0.006 m. 10-min averaged arc-max concentrations at 1.5 m height. STABILITY: set to D-E (intermediate class) as stated in the citation (Barad 1958 run 29: stability D-E); the unified model interpolates the dispersion coefficients. Obukhov length from the run's 7-level wind and temperature profiles (Barad 1958, Vol. I Table 8.1, digitised by J.S. Irwin) by the profile method with the Dyer (1974) / Paulson (1970) relations, z0 = 0.006 m.",
